Sources: src/libmpg123/{layer2.c,l2tables.h,l12tabs.h,tabinit.c,
dct64_neon64_float.S,synth_neon64_float.S,synth_real.c} in
https://www.mpg123.de/download/mpg123-1.33.7.tar.bz2

Modifications: safe Rust, mono fixed-header AHX subset only; scalar DCT
translation and explicitly fused multiply-add retain the aarch64 reference
arithmetic on other CPUs. Standard builds use f32::mul_add; allocation-free
no_std builds use libm 0.2.16 (MIT), with its default architecture paths
disabled. All state is owned, bounded, and streaming. No native code,
FFI, runtime CPU dispatch, resampling, or gapless trimming is used.

dct.rs and tables.rs were generated from these pinned sources by
scripts/generate_mpg123.py, then formatted with rustfmt. The generation is an
offline maintenance aid, not a build step or production dependency.

AHX framing and PCM16 conversion were checked against vgmstream r2117
src/meta/ahx.c, src/coding/mpeg_custom_utils_ahx.c, src/base/sbuf.c.
Its copyright and permission notice is preserved in LICENSE.vgmstream.

The test input and PCM golden file are synthetic and may be redistributed.
The PCM fixture was generated with the pinned aarch64 vgmstream/mpg123 build.
